---
import LegalLayout from '../components/LegalLayout.astro';
import PrivacyCenter from '../components/privacy/PrivacyCenter.astro';
import PrivacyRequestForm from '../components/privacy/PrivacyRequestForm.astro';
import { CONTACT, EMAILS } from '../config';
import { hasNonEssential, productionTrackers } from '../lib/privacy/registry';

/* The statement under "Where things stand today" is generated from the tool
   registry (src/lib/privacy/registry.ts), so it cannot say "nothing optional
   runs" once a tool is added. */
const tools = productionTrackers();
// Tools that wait for a yes; WellPeps' own anonymous statistics run by default with an opt-out.
const optionalToolsExist = hasNonEssential(tools);
const anonymousStatsLive = tools.some((t) => t.anonymous === true);

const clientNeeds = [
  'A privacy-request email address (we recommend privacy@wellpeps.com). Until you choose one, requests go to the general address below.',
  'Who inside your company owns these requests and makes sure they are handled on time (10 business days to confirm, 15 to act on an opt-out, 45 to answer an access or delete request).',
  'Whether a toll-free number is required for opt-out requests in the states you serve (your lawyer decides). No phone line is live today.',
];

/* Interim channel until a dedicated privacy mailbox exists. */
const privacyEmail = EMAILS.privacy;
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Your Privacy Choices"
  description="Choose how WellPeps uses your information: turn optional tools on or off, limit sensitive information, withdraw consent, and make privacy requests."
  subtitle="You decide how WellPeps uses your information. This page lists your choices and shows how to use them. It applies to everyone in the United States, whatever state you live in."
  clientNeeds={clientNeeds}
>
  <div class="callout callout--note">
    <strong>What is built and what is switched off</strong>
    <p>
      <span class="ph ph--web">Web team:</span> the switches, Global Privacy Control handling and the request form below work in
      the browser today. Server-side recording of choices (consent log) and online delivery of requests are written but not
      switched on until their Supabase functions are deployed; until then choices are kept in the visitor&rsquo;s browser and
      requests go out as a pre-filled email. Remove this box when both are live.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where things stand today</h2>
  {optionalToolsExist || anonymousStatsLive ? (
    <p>
      {optionalToolsExist && 'wellpeps.com uses a small number of optional tools. They stay off until you say yes, and you can turn them off again below. The tools are listed under each switch. '}
      {anonymousStatsLive && 'Our own anonymous usage statistics set no cookie and keep no identifier, so they cannot identify you. They are on by default, and you can turn them off below.'}
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      wellpeps.com does not sell your personal information and does not share it for targeted advertising. It does not use
      analytics or advertising tools, so there is nothing to switch off today. The switches below are ready: if we ever add
      such a tool, it will stay off until you turn it on.
      <span class="ph ph--web">Web team: confirm the same is true for portal.wellpeps.com and checkout before publishing this sentence.</span>
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    Each switch applies the moment you change it, and the page shows what is running right now. Your choice is saved in this
    browser for twelve months, or until we change this notice. On pages about health topics, analytics and advertising run only if
    you separately allow them there; "Accept all" does not include advertising on those pages.
  </p>

  <PrivacyCenter variant="page" idPrefix="pg" />

  <h2 id="gpc">Global Privacy Control</h2>
  <p>
    Global Privacy Control (GPC) is a browser setting, or an extension you can add, that tells websites you want to opt out of
    sale, sharing and targeted advertising. We honor it. When your browser sends the signal, we turn advertising off before any
    tool loads, tell you we detected it, and keep it off. If the signal conflicts with a choice you made on our site, we follow
    the signal and ask whether you want to allow advertising anyway.
  </p>

  <h2>Limit the use of your sensitive information</h2>
  <p>
    Health information is sensitive personal information. We use it only to provide the services you asked for, keep our
    systems secure, prevent fraud and meet legal duties. We do not use it for advertising without your separate, explicit
    consent. If you want us to keep our use to that
    and nothing more, ask using the form below and we will record your choice and honor it. Protected health information held by
    the medical practice is covered by the <a href="/notice-of-privacy-practices">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Withdraw your consent</h2>
  <p>
    Some health-related information is collected or shared with your consent, for example the topic of a free guide tied to your
    email address. You can take that consent back at any time using the form below. Withdrawing does not undo what happened
    before. To take back a permission you gave the medical practice for protected health information, follow the Notice of
    Privacy Practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Access, correct, delete, copy and appeal</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see what we hold about you, get a portable copy, correct it or delete it. If we say no in whole or in part,
    you can appeal, and a person who did not decide the first request will review it. Records held by the medical practice are
    covered by the Notice of Privacy Practices.
  </p>

  <h2>How to make a request</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Online:</strong> use the form below.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Mail:</strong> WellPeps, a Wyoming corporation, Attn: Privacy, 30 N Gould St., Suite R, Sheridan, WY 82801
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Phone:</strong> <a href="tel:+13078818700">(307) 881-8700</a> (normal business hours)
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>How we check it is you.</strong> We match what you tell us with what we hold, and we may send a link to your email
    address. We do not ask for your Social Security number. Opting out, limiting, withdrawing and unsubscribing need less
    checking than access or deletion.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>How fast.</strong> We confirm we received your request within 10 business days. We act on opt-outs, limits,
    withdrawals and unsubscribes within 15 business days. We answer access, correction, deletion and copy requests within 45
    days, and we may extend once by up to 45 days and tell you why. There is no charge.
    <span class="ph ph--legal">Lawyer: confirm these periods by state.</span>
  </p>

  <PrivacyRequestForm privacyEmail={privacyEmail} />

  <h2>Authorized agents</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask another person to make a request for you. We will ask for your signed permission, or a power of attorney, and
    may confirm with you directly.
  </p>

  <h2>No unfair treatment</h2>
  <p>
    We will not deny you service, charge you a different price or give you lower quality because you used a privacy choice.
  </p>

  <h2>More information</h2>
  <p>
    Read the <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, the Consumer Health Data Privacy Policy, the Cookie and Tracking
    Technologies Notice and the <a href="/notice-of-privacy-practices">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
